pocketchip-batt (0.5) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Replace the 2 s bash/i2cget/bc oneshot timer with a long-running C
    service that reads /sys/class/power_supply/axp20x-battery, keeps the
    (sample + average) / 2 voltage average, and rewrites
    /run/pocketchip-batt/{voltage,charging} only when a value changes.
    Charger plug/unplug uevents resample the charging state immediately.
  * /usr/lib/pocketchip-batt/{voltage,charging} are now symlinks into
    /run/pocketchip-batt, so the readers are unchanged and nothing is
    written to NAND.
  * Drop pocketchip-batt.timer; stop and disable it on upgrade.
  * Add a fake-sysfs test suite run by dh_auto_test; debhelper compat 13.

 -- Josh Bailey <josh@vandervecken.com>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 23:30:00 +0000

pocketchip-batt (0.4) trixie; urgency=low

  * warn05/warn15: replace the unbounded busy-loop that read voltage with a
    single read + safe-high default (3700). On an empty/missing voltage file the
    old `while [ -z "$VOLT" ]` loop never exited, so the oneshot warn services
    spun until systemd's start-timeout and were marked FAILED.
  * warn05/warn15 + warn-clean.service: `rm` -> `rm -f` so removing an absent
    flag file (the common case) no longer fails the unit; added a trailing
    `exit 0` to the warn scripts.
  * pocketchip-batt poller: validate the bc result and write voltage atomically
    (temp + mv) so it never leaves an empty voltage file for the warn readers.

 -- Ben Young <computermouth@proton.me>  Thu, 18 Jun 2026 02:30:00 -0500

